{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "1ce2cd59-0598-41f8-87c0-3cc18422132a",
    "name": "restaurant_tables_api",
    "description": "Full API surface of the restaurant-table-reservation API Gateway (HTTP, port 3000).\n\nRun order: the folders are numbered. Requests marked (auto-captures ...) save ids/token into collection variables, so running the folders in order (or a Collection Runner pass over the whole collection) chains together without manual copy-paste.\n\nPrerequisites:\n- infra: docker compose up -d   (Postgres + Kafka)\n- services: npm run dev         (api-gateway, auth, restaurant, table, reservation, notification, email)\n\nCollection-level auth is Bearer {{token}}; public endpoints override it with noauth.\n\nIdempotency: the important POST routes accept an `Idempotency-Key` header. Retrying with the same key (same user, method and path) replays the stored response rather than repeating the side effect. See folder \"8. Idempotency (replay demo)\". The header is optional today - omitting it runs the request normally.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "11981962",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/11981962-1ce2cd59-0598-41f8-87c0-3cc18422132a?source=collection_link"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
